;; fault-access-ld.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-access-ld.s` (P2-SCALAR.3).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py fault-access-ld.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "fault-access-ld.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `fault-access-ld.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). The load access-fault rule carried INTO the three-way comparison: guest-no-device pins" "the same rule at 0x0200_BFF8, but that address is spike's built-in CLINT (its spike comparison is" "disabled); 0x40000000 is no platform's device. x1 is never written.")
(expectations (program "fault-access-ld.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (never_written "x1") (step (n 0) (insn "lui x11, 0x40000") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "0x40000 << 12 = 0x40000000; bit 31 is clear, so the sign extension adds nothing. The address is outside sail-riscv's MainMemory region, outside spike's DRAM, and no device on either platform — the reason this guest can run cross-model where guest-no-device cannot.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4 (D-LUI-AUIPC)")) (step (n 1) (insn "ld x1, x11, 0") (writes) (derivation "The effective address 0x40000000 is outside every declared region, so the load raises an access-fault exception, and x1 is never written — the negative observation a serviced load would fail. Measured on both references: cause 0x05, tval 0x0000000040000000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.3; RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (D-ADDRESS-SPACE: an access outside a declared region raises an access-fault exception)")))
